  'Investigate one consequential “big problem” through multiple disciplinary lenses, integrate diverse evidence into a more comprehensive understanding, and collaborate with relevant publics to create an ethical, useful, and well-communicated contribution.',
  $intpjson${"slug": "interdisciplinary-topics-course", "title": "Interdisciplinary Topics Course", "description": "Investigate one consequential “big problem” through multiple disciplinary lenses, integrate diverse evidence into a more comprehensive understanding, and collaborate with relevant publics to create an ethical, useful, and well-communicated contribution.", "topics": [{"id": "3607e0e3-45a4-4d78-a6e9-b50b636f8cc3", "type": "topic", "title": "The Big Question: Defining the Topic and the Problem", "description": "Interdisciplinary inquiry starts with a problem that cannot be understood adequately through one field alone. Students learn to turn a broad theme into a researchable, consequential question with boundaries, stakeholders, and a shared vocabulary.", "children": [{"id": "8a458d9f-9e3a-434e-8b9b-e0faba6362f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Theme and problem space", "children": [{"id": "2297ed0d-0ccf-48bd-9e35-76e6542247dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Possible themes: climate resilience, AI and society, migration, public health, democracy, or urban futures"}, {"id": "ac286a7e-ac70-4414-8c54-a23020ec3aea", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem situations, symptoms, causes, consequences, and contested meanings"}, {"id": "b993113e-2876-46e0-84d8-cf8d8f11b4dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Why the problem exceeds a single discipline"}], "description": "Distinguish a compelling topic from a specific problem that can guide sustained inquiry."}, {"id": "2613ad0b-a52f-4410-bc03-a19fc7625e75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Question formulation", "children": [{"id": "f9bde134-8503-4827-8083-4e527541ac19", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, causal, interpretive, normative, and design questions"}, {"id": "038f0632-85ed-4ff3-afd3-7c252d36f10d", "type": "concept", "title": "Question scope, feasibility, significance, and uncertainty"}, {"id": "16334424-b080-42f2-b7e1-564c8dc92052", "type": "concept", "title": "Nested questions and a shared inquiry agenda"}], "description": "Develop questions that invite explanation, interpretation, evaluation, and action."}, {"id": "0c0f5cc6-aff4-4630-b7d2-b29f431456c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Boundaries and scale", "children": [{"id": "7f4eae34-a740-415c-92ee-af8f431cedad", "type": "concept", "title": "Local, regional, national, planetary, and historical scales"}, {"id": "2b4b7dfa-6d4e-4dea-8608-f952fb4cb20f", "type": "concept", "title": "Population, institution, ecosystem, technology, and time boundaries"}, {"id": "46e44398-4e42-4dfa-9257-f2640cce0379", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundary choices, exclusions, and implications"}], "description": "Decide where the study begins and ends without pretending the problem is isolated."}, {"id": "0c1f41f1-c9b1-4e4d-8e86-27f583bbdeb7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stakeholders and publics", "children": [{"id": "fcf0682f-9439-4f9b-8ea1-c94ff1f083e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Affected communities, decision makers, experts, organizations, and nonhuman interests"}, {"id": "5d02a565-7ea7-45df-b693-a10c81887709", "type": "concept", "title": "Power, voice, incentives, responsibilities, and conflicts"}, {"id": "cace1a00-388b-4389-8e86-2ee6b15f58bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder maps and engagement priorities"}], "description": "Identify who experiences, defines, governs, studies, or can change the problem."}, {"id": "d2b636fc-f110-4c30-8959-df8b1b0a82a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inquiry charter", "children": [{"id": "ed14ca52-621e-4680-b2d3-50a811d875f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Central question, subquestions, outcomes, and audience"}, {"id": "96882ef3-80ac-4418-931b-c46ea1a05bdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Assumptions, terms, unknowns, and success criteria"}, {"id": "5146fca9-1857-44e6-aa5e-5793f1837cd9", "type": "concept", "title": "Research ethics, team norms, milestones, and revision process"}], "description": "Create a living agreement about purpose, evidence, collaboration, and deliverables."}]}, {"id": "03f75b1f-7dc1-4947-9ecb-887d5666c7d4", "type": "topic", "title": "Disciplines, Epistemologies, and Ways of Knowing", "description": "Disciplines are not simply collections of facts; they organize questions, methods, evidence, values, and standards of explanation. Students learn to recognize these architectures so that integration respects real differences rather than flattening them.", "children": [{"id": "def16e24-e29d-4612-b08a-ed5557e64385", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Anatomy of a discipline", "children": [{"id": "05b9639f-baab-4a2c-adac-76ddca905fa4", "type": "concept", "title": "Objects of study and characteristic questions"}, {"id": "2aa4df97-9674-44a6-bf9f-d8c043481dae", "type": "concept", "title": "Core concepts, theories, methods, genres, and institutions"}, {"id": "66c6e693-8cad-497d-adfd-9e30f78d0a0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards of evidence, explanation, and expertise"}], "description": "Examine how fields define legitimate problems and knowledge."}, {"id": "50260d02-cba2-4ef3-ba95-f7758c44ae46", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Epistemologies", "children": [{"id": "be2c24e6-3e13-49bc-be25-6b16fe67a2a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Empiricism, interpretation, rationalism, pragmatism, and critical approaches"}, {"id": "367ac869-8e58-4abe-861f-31fd282154a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Objectivity, situated knowledge, standpoint, and reflexivity"}, {"id": "7b0dc2c1-5421-4bd7-8bc3-87d89e50b18b", "type": "concept", "title": "Certainty, probability, ambiguity, and pluralism"}], "description": "Compare accounts of what can be known and how claims become warranted."}, {"id": "eb7883dc-b9a5-46df-a930-6133c478fc8e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Paradigms and assumptions", "children": [{"id": "f13d6b61-5d9d-4781-a9f1-800ca5a5b722", "type": "concept", "title": "Ontology, causality, agency, structure, and scale"}, {"id": "b7ade903-6e6e-48c3-b23b-6d209d3a7082", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual, institutional, cultural, ecological, and technological explanations"}, {"id": "0ea036f1-7c72-45e4-b605-1ccde04a522f", "type": "concept", "title": "Normal science, anomalies, and paradigm change"}], "description": "Surface commitments that are often invisible within a field."}, {"id": "7698a4e7-58f8-427e-972e-ac4af02b9fdc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multi-, inter-, and transdisciplinarity", "children": [{"id": "e5f7bbc9-9aea-4dc6-b478-e891be75c3a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Multidisciplinary juxtaposition"}, {"id": "f7b27ece-4585-4e37-ab86-5216f2217917", "type": "concept", "title": "Interdisciplinary synthesis"}, {"id": "7841489c-8ca7-4494-86a6-c0b5861ff1ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Transdisciplinary collaboration with practitioners and communities"}], "description": "Differentiate parallel contributions from genuine integration and co-production."}, {"id": "660913ec-4f0b-4af2-bd8c-7df52ffce4a9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intellectual humility", "children": [{"id": "4aa2b85f-fec7-4177-8d30-de47e8d8889b", "type": "concept", "title": "Competence boundaries and responsible borrowing"}, {"id": "88b5d870-5ab2-4477-b470-7945bc55bd69", "type": "concept", "title": "Translation without caricature"}, {"id": "377047a1-1e20-4386-b11a-a821d2f62c59", "type": "concept", "title": "Productive disagreement and revisable conclusions"}], "description": "Treat expertise as necessary but partial."}]}, {"id": "88a60149-f800-4d19-813f-bc87a696fec3", "type": "topic", "title": "Humanities Lenses: Meaning, History, Culture, and Interpretation", "description": "Humanities methods reveal how language, memory, values, narratives, and cultural forms shape complex problems. Students learn to analyze meaning and historical possibility rather than treating present conditions as natural or inevitable.", "children": [{"id": "bd1cb5f9-5d1c-4e7d-ac95-8c8273d91f62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical inquiry", "children": [{"id": "0085c64c-e340-49f7-b698-bf3bcd1bec20", "type": "concept", "title": "Periodization, chronology, and turning points"}, {"id": "f9dfb0d5-1f16-4ac4-b9d0-6e956b40f53a", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and secondary sources"}, {"id": "663784e1-73ec-4177-a7de-f72cd35b4926", "type": "concept", "title": "Archives, silences, and historiography"}], "description": "Trace change, continuity, contingency, and path dependence."}, {"id": "7e433cf9-e22b-44ba-8d1d-72873e13bc6c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Textual and rhetorical analysis", "children": [{"id": "3e00ff98-d33f-48a9-9704-172bfcd881a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Close reading and contextual interpretation"}, {"id": "29f5b998-3a65-4408-8a63-37e18443da4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Metaphor, framing, genre, argument, and audience"}, {"id": "fe546bee-871c-4b4c-8fd2-955ecb08a334", "type": "concept", "title": "Public discourse, policy language, and media narratives"}], "description": "Study how language constructs problems, identities, and possible actions."}, {"id": "1e145080-2960-45c1-b73a-2526b437e71b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cultural analysis", "children": [{"id": "84f71dfa-39c6-45e2-a315-c70379f24293", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation, identity, ritual, memory, and ideology"}, {"id": "4c620dc1-9fa5-4f8a-aa4d-816afde42d53", "type": "concept", "title": "Popular culture, material culture, and digital culture"}, {"id": "8453b4e0-7bc7-4f8e-9f43-ab5dfd4e1a1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Dominant, residual, emergent, and countercultural forms"}], "description": "Interpret symbols, practices, institutions, and everyday life."}, {"id": "14548717-472c-4d0e-a75a-fc58bcfb05db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Philosophical analysis", "children": [{"id": "882acf20-34d0-4222-83a1-82a52b5f7283", "type": "concept", "title": "Conceptual distinctions and thought experiments"}, {"id": "d6879176-c17f-4fa2-becf-4fb03a8f7a96", "type": "concept", "title": "Normative theories and practical ethics"}, {"id": "dd4c395c-bb1f-4e59-b25d-aea1b3c7de62", "type": "concept", "title": "Logic, counterargument, and reflective equilibrium"}], "description": "Clarify concepts and evaluate reasons, values, and obligations."}, {"id": "0d76129d-d050-4006-b55e-28c497661618", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Creative and imaginative knowledge", "children": [{"id": "23648f30-feff-4a1e-8e68-0f4713f9034b", "type": "concept", "title": "Literature, visual art, performance, and film as evidence or inquiry"}, {"id": "1b796ecd-c18c-478f-b113-ac4d7b552c9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Speculative fiction and alternative futures"}, {"id": "36562d23-e9d2-4c7f-819a-d6a69097821d", "type": "concept", "title": "Aesthetic form, empathy, estrangement, and interpretation"}], "description": "Use art and narrative to explore experience, possibility, and moral attention."}]}, {"id": "60875113-f172-4f0c-9961-6304a53034fc", "type": "topic", "title": "Social Science Lenses: Institutions, Behavior, Power, and Society", "description": "Social sciences connect individual action to groups, institutions, markets, policies, and cultures. Students compare explanatory models and learn to combine qualitative and quantitative evidence without confusing association with cause.", "children": [{"id": "22579864-2e96-4647-82f2-133df96c8b39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Levels of social explanation", "children": [{"id": "ac986965-c208-4d6c-b957-062913538412", "type": "concept", "title": "Micro, meso, and macro levels"}, {"id": "f88743fd-37fb-4d60-91ea-124e20e0f4fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency, structure, norms, incentives, and identity"}, {"id": "265c7370-5be5-4804-8dca-283d43f0e912", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback between individual and collective outcomes"}], "description": "Locate mechanisms across persons, networks, organizations, and institutions."}, {"id": "eb371b0d-9a17-4c30-ab60-91bc3cb4f094", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutions and governance", "children": [{"id": "de32633c-7109-4615-80e4-a985a90138b3", "type": "concept", "title": "States, markets, firms, schools, families, and civil society"}, {"id": "f1ec7860-9590-4d81-a201-72b976aa5618", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy design, implementation, and administrative capacity"}, {"id": "cfd608b4-51b9-4610-9a1a-71026ce75855", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional change, lock-in, and legitimacy"}], "description": "Analyze how formal and informal rules distribute authority and resources."}, {"id": "5398a17f-8e60-44cc-a419-19c2696d551f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Power and inequality", "children": [{"id": "74afdd13-cb86-4492-92e9-f58578c127e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Class, race, gender, disability, citizenship, and intersectionality"}, {"id": "dc588487-b683-465c-866c-4a4bf986379f", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural, relational, discursive, and coercive power"}, {"id": "6e7ffee5-4afb-4d91-bf37-d56249844ef8", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement, lived experience, and cumulative disadvantage"}], "description": "Examine how benefits, burdens, recognition, and voice are distributed."}, {"id": "38042057-f16a-481c-8146-ac8d5c27d42b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Behavior and decision making", "children": [{"id": "31b53e74-dc8a-4320-8724-48e0c3efdc2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Preferences, incentives, heuristics, and biases"}, {"id": "6a044e4e-5e67-4c10-ab40-15134d21c8db", "type": "concept", "title": "Social norms, networks, identity, and collective action"}, {"id": "c87a88a0-5430-4530-a6d1-db0010c738a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Experiments, surveys, observational studies, and limitations"}], "description": "Study choice in social context rather than assuming fully rational actors."}, {"id": "e02e022d-f602-43d7-8a2f-df0e90a095d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Causal and comparative reasoning", "children": [{"id": "55353d05-1259-44d5-99da-9904b63172dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Correlation, mechanism, confounding, and counterfactuals"}, {"id": "a2152e0d-52d8-470e-943e-cf033b3ad865", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative case selection"}, {"id": "ada7b3ce-1ee5-4311-881f-8c8abd457170", "type": "concept", "title": "Generalization, context, and external validity"}], "description": "Evaluate why outcomes differ across groups, places, institutions, or time."}]}, {"id": "34fca065-59f4-4b10-bc95-8036ef882572", "type": "topic", "title": "Natural and Quantitative Lenses: Systems, Measurement, and Evidence", "description": "Scientific and quantitative approaches help characterize mechanisms, patterns, constraints, and uncertainty. Students learn to use numbers critically—checking definitions, models, uncertainty, and values embedded in measurement.", "children": [{"id": "4f19591c-7602-4b1d-bae8-6ce1becfaacb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scientific modeling", "children": [{"id": "a20ac08a-1d5d-4134-8b1f-6045c9676181", "type": "concept", "title": "Variables, mechanisms, assumptions, boundaries, and scales"}, {"id": "06a2e984-31c7-4871-bcdc-fb51622fd816", "type": "concept", "title": "Conceptual, mathematical, computational, and physical models"}, {"id": "bccadfbd-b2e6-427e-b44c-67caefec275b", "type": "concept", "title": "Model validation, limitations, and domain of applicability"}], "description": "Represent selected features of reality to explain or predict."}, {"id": "7312ff2a-f6dd-44a4-8f1b-754ddf26e24d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Measurement and indicators", "children": [{"id": "f2e8915a-670d-438a-a71d-9895a579904b", "type": "concept", "title": "Operational definitions, units, validity, and reliability"}, {"id": "02f19da2-bff1-4253-ae11-dfc264b5060a", "type": "concept", "title": "Proxies, composite indicators, baselines, and denominators"}, {"id": "d7341517-eb93-45ae-b5ca-952d39e81958", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement error and missing data"}], "description": "Ask what a number represents, how it was produced, and what it excludes."}, {"id": "aee53cb9-b85b-4872-bc02-209a578774a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data interpretation", "children": [{"id": "da644f46-73b6-4f52-ae93-6acd8dda3b60", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributions, rates, uncertainty intervals, and effect sizes"}, {"id": "5173db02-84fb-4ecb-b535-9ed4eeb39563", "type": "concept", "title": "Correlation, causation, selection, and survivorship"}, {"id": "a865edc9-1f0f-4aad-8828-2de0b020541f", "type": "concept", "title": "Visualization choices and misleading comparisons"}], "description": "Read patterns while resisting overclaiming."}, {"id": "044b68c7-b628-4866-b7f5-17598a495344", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ecological and planetary constraints", "children": [{"id": "8fd4cfa4-3741-40fd-8ffb-70e4ccea7977", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy and material flows"}, {"id": "c4a1320a-5d0a-49a8-9974-b953f3b0f0b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecosystems, resilience, thresholds, and feedback"}, {"id": "be0cb7fc-606d-4519-a11f-53d26f2b5c96", "type": "concept", "title": "Climate, biodiversity, pollution, and resource use"}], "description": "Connect human systems to biophysical processes and limits."}, {"id": "66475f0c-9f90-4a99-ab8a-0476cf48d01c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quantification and values", "children": [{"id": "646a7781-0652-4892-af8f-0de2ddbc40b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefit, harm, risk, and quality-of-life metrics"}, {"id": "76882da4-3921-4b6a-9b72-745378b8a111", "type": "concept", "title": "Monetization and nonmonetary values"}, {"id": "471c3268-095f-460d-bfb9-c4a1d24bd029", "type": "concept", "title": "Distribution, uncertainty, and ethical limits of aggregation"}], "description": "Recognize that deciding what to count is partly normative."}]}, {"id": "12d69e6c-462d-4bad-bcae-c9507e2a41a0", "type": "topic", "title": "Arts, Design, and Creative Practice as Inquiry", "description": "Creative practice can generate knowledge, reveal experience, and prototype alternatives. Students learn to use design and artistic methods alongside—not merely after—analysis.", "children": [{"id": "0465a89d-76a9-4477-9045-05ce6a2c4fb0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Practice-based inquiry", "children": [{"id": "a69e05d0-7c3d-45dc-9981-ab029f3d9cca", "type": "concept", "title": "Sketching, composing, performance, fabrication, and iteration"}, {"id": "a4f55be8-202f-42fb-a10a-ae00309bb3e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Process documentation and reflective commentary"}, {"id": "15e7af25-9327-4f73-9d9b-4846e3b9c5b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Tacit, embodied, sensory, and experiential knowledge"}], "description": "Treat making as a disciplined process of questioning and discovery."}, {"id": "826e3304-d034-4d22-925d-8bd00d37026d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Human-centered research", "children": [{"id": "d815e015-84b4-497f-98a3-1662147f4310", "type": "concept", "title": "Observation, interviews, journey maps, and cultural probes"}, {"id": "91cbf49e-3a96-4043-bdf5-e7ebc49bf246", "type": "concept", "title": "Extreme users, accessibility, and inclusive participation"}, {"id": "d80d2264-f9bc-4ff2-bf0a-e73bc15bb117", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, reciprocity, and avoiding extractive research"}], "description": "Understand needs and contexts through direct engagement."}, {"id": "facc9f3a-ad41-4bb9-8834-3ed0793426c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Problem reframing", "children": [{"id": "bd7e95b7-23ea-4bb8-b6d3-c1383659b24f", "type": "concept", "title": "How-might-we questions and assumption reversal"}, {"id": "0cfda1c4-20f6-4c45-82b9-669be036e6cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Needs, values, functions, and systemic causes"}, {"id": "bb735a72-cfbd-493b-abbd-145215fbcfaa", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternative framings and their consequences"}], "description": "Challenge inherited definitions and expand the space of possibilities."}, {"id": "a77dbe9e-71d8-4522-82c6-a1bcd125c478", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ideation and prototyping", "children": [{"id": "85647dc9-41b1-4938-ab42-eb3f5b044893", "type": "concept", "title": "Divergence, analogy, combination, and co-creation"}, {"id": "5f657ba2-9e83-4858-b5d4-362c87906feb", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-fidelity prototypes, storyboards, scenarios, and role-play"}, {"id": "0a81fcd6-a9a5-49a1-adf2-52f932f2d8fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback, iteration, and learning goals"}], "description": "Make ideas tangible enough to test and discuss."}, {"id": "8d4d91e3-8e09-498d-8acd-ea81cc94f807", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation and public imagination", "children": [{"id": "56bee263-ed02-4d28-af5e-35f26b78f574", "type": "concept", "title": "Exhibitions, maps, installations, documentary, and interactive media"}, {"id": "5e73781f-ffbc-4b8e-94e7-df7ad7c6b386", "type": "concept", "title": "Counter-narratives and speculative design"}, {"id": "79faf836-7fd0-4216-bdf7-a5aa082420e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience experience, accessibility, and interpretation"}], "description": "Use form and media to shape attention and collective possibility."}]}, {"id": "1e0a05f0-801b-42c5-84b4-03738fb6a803", "type": "topic", "title": "Evidence Literacy and Mixed-Methods Research", "description": "World-class interdisciplinary work is methodologically plural but not methodologically vague. Students learn to locate, assess, combine, and document qualitative, quantitative, historical, and creative evidence.", "children": [{"id": "7b3b9a28-6984-4d89-9c20-4a7ce8c99c45", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research strategy", "children": [{"id": "5d0965e3-10f2-41ce-b2f2-23894532105d", "type": "concept", "title": "Exploratory, descriptive, explanatory, evaluative, and design research"}, {"id": "9911055a-4c20-4bb6-a43a-fa235e20379e", "type": "concept", "title": "Case study, comparative, experimental, ethnographic, archival, and mixed-methods designs"}, {"id": "336b7a78-a879-4953-a0a7-ba31ae3bd13c", "type": "concept", "title": "Feasibility, access, ethics, and triangulation"}], "description": "Match questions to evidence and methods."}, {"id": "d94b5ea9-127c-42aa-9d43-742dac3b7cae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Source discovery and provenance", "children": [{"id": "e4a9a6e3-0cf6-4c04-bdcd-dd2c8b69782d", "type": "concept", "title": "Scholarly databases, archives, datasets, policy documents, and community knowledge"}, {"id": "5936f298-3140-49b2-a8f8-1683da61d676", "type": "concept", "title": "Citation chaining, controlled vocabulary, and grey literature"}, {"id": "994fc4f0-44be-4b42-9cea-2c091784a947", "type": "concept", "title": "Authorship, funding, version, date, and data lineage"}], "description": "Build a transparent evidence base across disciplines."}, {"id": "1c2081fb-0cf6-4753-8c9f-8d9feea8763b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical appraisal", "children": [{"id": "22e39e53-16bf-4ce1-8805-5a50551b3745", "type": "concept", "title": "Credibility, relevance, validity, reliability, and bias"}, {"id": "fcf3eb2c-efcb-40b9-a124-c15deebc417d", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer review, replication, saturation, and corroboration"}, {"id": "0844955c-4523-4c7c-a73e-b15cb18c3f35", "type": "concept", "title": "Expert consensus, disagreement, and uncertainty"}], "description": "Evaluate evidence using standards appropriate to its source and claim."}, {"id": "bca65af8-f40b-4654-8dd8-fe109a8581aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mixed-methods integration", "children": [{"id": "d3c52a52-9cde-4b5c-a9f8-dd93cee3b422", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequential, concurrent, and embedded designs"}, {"id": "0835883b-a6fc-4940-99c1-691db2d0ec75", "type": "concept", "title": "Convergence, complementarity, expansion, and contradiction"}, {"id": "e60d7cf0-a31a-43e7-8dd0-a985d0cc518b", "type": "concept", "title": "Joint displays and integrated interpretation"}], "description": "Use methods to answer complementary parts of the problem."}, {"id": "85ce0ba8-a758-4a2d-bb8b-d2282fef1c39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research transparency", "children": [{"id": "3807bf38-8b55-4d77-8ccd-d3d09bd00883", "type": "concept", "title": "Search logs, coding decisions, analytic memos, and data dictionaries"}, {"id": "64b803a2-00ac-4efd-9cba-e3bb5bbd5c69", "type": "concept", "title": "Citation management and reproducible workflows"}, {"id": "49c7f9ad-9601-46be-a3b3-b169662e315f", "type": "concept", "title": "Open materials, privacy, intellectual property, and limitations"}], "description": "Make the path from source to conclusion inspectable."}]}, {"id": "63e801ba-d5e9-445f-8a0e-001849eb5e5f", "type": "topic", "title": "Systems Thinking, Complexity, and Mapping", "description": "Complex problems emerge from interactions, feedback, delays, adaptation, and multiple scales. Students learn to map systems without mistaking the map for the world and to identify leverage, tradeoffs, and unintended consequences.", "children": [{"id": "069264af-7930-4fca-bd35-fd060b56c150", "type": "subtopic", "title": "System structure", "children": [{"id": "6cbc8523-c282-4ebc-a5f8-e57328e159cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Stocks, flows, actors, institutions, technologies, and environments"}, {"id": "e7a709c0-c5eb-4589-a371-3900971e305c", "type": "concept", "title": "Material, information, financial, and influence connections"}, {"id": "c62d9434-96df-472c-8463-2835b77ca093", "type": "concept", "title": "Nested systems and boundary critique"}], "description": "Define elements, relationships, purpose, and boundary."}, {"id": "afb654df-bfb0-408a-a9bd-f4b6a8159525", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Feedback and dynamics", "children": [{"id": "46846b6c-ccd0-4555-9ece-a3fc65d259dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Reinforcing and balancing loops"}, {"id": "94d49948-3687-4097-b303-e1a9c1ec6eda", "type": "concept", "title": "Delays, accumulation, nonlinearity, and oscillation"}, {"id": "dd36dbfd-b859-4614-b191-78fe54c18fcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Path dependence, lock-in, and tipping behavior"}], "description": "Explain how circular causality creates persistence or change."}, {"id": "17290319-fe3f-4071-a092-e06c4f279050", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Networks and emergence", "children": [{"id": "ad1cce04-4567-4061-802b-416914634d3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Nodes, ties, centrality, clustering, and diffusion concepts"}, {"id": "bceb699e-68b6-4146-848c-113724cd2d4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Local rules and emergent outcomes"}, {"id": "79a9af60-69af-4d05-af63-b886fc76ffb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Contagion, coordination, polarization, and resilience"}], "description": "Study patterns that arise from distributed interaction."}, {"id": "3587ddf7-cdd1-4ed0-9034-8b53b97505ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Complex adaptive systems", "children": [{"id": "4b9437fc-df62-4b2b-9993-28cbfe89429e", "type": "concept", "title": "Agents, variation, selection, and adaptation"}, {"id": "fcf941df-7b36-4083-8e16-8932de69bd77", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-organization and regime shifts"}, {"id": "52398aeb-568b-46f7-b2ad-646e6d893486", "type": "concept", "title": "Prediction limits and scenario thinking"}], "description": "Recognize learning, adaptation, heterogeneity, and coevolution."}, {"id": "febec7f9-88e5-4a21-9f4e-f1b80d3f2e23", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Leverage and unintended effects", "children": [{"id": "8fa2026d-8a74-4ae2-aafc-73f889fd74ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Parameters, information, rules, goals, and paradigms"}, {"id": "2434f5ab-b52f-46e0-8962-e4eb075091d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Second-order effects and policy resistance"}, {"id": "e7b30a37-8047-4020-8cf1-cc1ac3d2efc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Robust portfolios and monitoring signals"}], "description": "Identify interventions while examining who gains, who loses, and what might rebound."}]}, {"id": "91eca66b-4276-447a-9f9f-8ffc568c8139", "type": "topic", "title": "Integration: Creating Common Ground and New Understanding", "description": "Integration is the defining intellectual work of interdisciplinarity. Students learn to connect insights by clarifying concepts, reconciling assumptions, relating mechanisms, and constructing a synthesis that changes how the problem is understood.", "children": [{"id": "a6460ff0-8908-4ba3-a706-1d47320a246e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict mapping", "children": [{"id": "662c39a8-e496-47ba-ba86-441c37eb31c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Different terms for similar ideas"}, {"id": "3ae8b5ab-b253-4bff-a385-670c7c6e74ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Same terms with different meanings"}, {"id": "31d5e5e1-92c0-4756-b821-575369bb24eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Differences in scale, unit of analysis, method, or value"}], "description": "Locate where disciplinary findings agree, complement, or contradict."}, {"id": "5263db01-99c1-49fd-9e2a-098d2d720b7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Concept clarification", "children": [{"id": "0bd71003-f5e8-44e9-bb1a-ff1abdc19eb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Definitions, dimensions, typologies, and boundary concepts"}, {"id": "e70424dd-88d6-4fa2-a64b-a8ebe5422f34", "type": "concept", "title": "Common ground and conceptual translation"}, {"id": "3920c550-3e77-4172-a99c-f0139cb51690", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundary objects and trading zones"}], "description": "Create enough shared language for collaboration without erasing productive difference."}, {"id": "28484c2c-d801-4f81-875f-1c51bd9aca6c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integration techniques", "children": [{"id": "326cf6ec-8168-4272-bfbf-26f788209a54", "type": "concept", "title": "Extension, redefinition, organization, transformation, and causal linkage"}, {"id": "657198b9-0e9f-4604-ba7d-3ba91ff0944b", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept maps, matrices, timelines, and multi-level models"}, {"id": "f9cbdbe6-60c4-43e0-8018-d1b88893bee3", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative, systems, and design synthesis"}], "description": "Combine disciplinary insights through explicit reasoning."}, {"id": "a2ee4bb9-2903-466d-891f-52e0f1231e03", "type": "subtopic", "title": "More-comprehensive understanding", "children": [{"id": "586ce664-1a20-483a-bdc3-7032dc8d5ae7", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-level mechanisms and interactions"}, {"id": "820dae38-b834-4c16-8e5b-1fff14a25217", "type": "concept", "title": "Tradeoffs, tensions, paradoxes, and conditional conclusions"}, {"id": "e20a1ad2-dc29-4952-956f-00fed1dca145", "type": "concept", "title": "Novel hypotheses, questions, and intervention points"}], "description": "Show what the integration explains that separate accounts do not."}, {"id": "eeb6954d-728b-4d6a-b3e5-a375064d8f4f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integration quality", "children": [{"id": "e7c8ed78-dead-4f9e-b280-78693b52fa69", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsiveness to each discipline’s strongest evidence"}, {"id": "b56a3f12-1a8e-45ea-9def-99e35bf53761", "type": "concept", "title": "Coherence, explanatory power, usefulness, and transparency"}, {"id": "ebdeb130-84f7-4504-abdc-dafa015997fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Residual disagreement and limits"}], "description": "Evaluate synthesis rather than rewarding mere breadth."}]}, {"id": "a6c0ea30-a345-42ec-b926-785264a9316c", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Power, Positionality, and Responsible Inquiry", "description": "Interdisciplinary projects make choices about whose knowledge counts, who bears risk, and what futures are desirable. Students learn to examine their own position, engage ethically, and make normative commitments visible.", "children": [{"id": "75d1865b-eace-43b5-87bf-e5b827b01578", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Positionality and reflexivity", "children": [{"id": "9482d64c-1847-48d0-b1e5-b726216ec197", "type": "concept", "title": "Researcher standpoint and access"}, {"id": "94aa4952-2f8e-4ac9-a678-84cc5d293184", "type": "concept", "title": "Insider/outsider roles"}, {"id": "225c799f-1efd-4387-b287-8a1ea7b0985b", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflexive journals and team discussion"}], "description": "Understand how identity, training, interests, and institutional location shape inquiry."}, {"id": "59566e67-6a94-418e-9684-1ee2f586e35e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research and engagement ethics", "children": [{"id": "a740a11b-7ed0-4d5f-857d-4998aedfa3de", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, confidentiality, privacy, and data stewardship"}, {"id": "ac5f461c-782e-4fb0-8951-16119bab556a", "type": "concept", "title": "Community knowledge, ownership, compensation, and attribution"}, {"id": "d7d8447b-2d79-4218-bfe1-3d540c23c131", "type": "concept", "title": "Human-subjects review and harm assessment"}], "description": "Protect people and communities while building reciprocal relationships."}, {"id": "abd60437-7739-404c-89a9-24ecc97f2563", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Justice frameworks", "children": [{"id": "2a097a15-27a1-49b3-b957-f5d58ce526b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Procedural, distributive, restorative, and intergenerational justice"}, {"id": "9ae8451b-89a5-47f1-b6c5-851239d5387f", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental, disability, racial, gender, and data justice"}, {"id": "3bceb33a-6c05-40aa-9823-8364cf19405e", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectionality and cumulative impacts"}], "description": "Evaluate distribution, recognition, participation, and capability."}, {"id": "98936213-b9aa-40cd-8cf1-4fda9cadc963", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Knowledge and power", "children": [{"id": "ce0bc7b0-25b5-4db0-b0c3-63acf2a96f8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Epistemic injustice and testimonial credibility"}, {"id": "819857d6-cb70-44bf-8fc5-d6bdffe3574d", "type": "concept", "title": "Coloniality, extraction, and Indigenous knowledge sovereignty"}, {"id": "a13559a8-3bd5-490c-940b-9f0ffcd5d8ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional expertise and democratic participation"}], "description": "Examine how expertise becomes authoritative and how alternatives are marginalized."}, {"id": "9dccd136-a4e6-45fd-9d55-425197900cd1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible recommendations", "children": [{"id": "10ca5742-0d58-4eea-a0fb-b8a0c75d3a8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefits, burdens, reversibility, and precaution"}, {"id": "c2be98fe-c6e8-493e-aef1-34dba3e463f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflicts of interest and accountability"}, {"id": "331054b8-60cf-481d-a131-5437c59bccc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Conditions, safeguards, monitoring, and avenues for redress"}], "description": "State values, uncertainties, and tradeoffs rather than hiding them behind technical language."}]}, {"id": "acb7a97f-2355-4da3-b623-e4f342911e5e", "type": "topic", "title": "Comparative Case Studies and Historical Context", "description": "Cases let students test concepts against real complexity. Comparison reveals patterns, causal mechanisms, contextual differences, and the danger of copying solutions without understanding where they came from.", "children": [{"id": "2cc844f3-69ab-4b53-bed6-c37eb140ac31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case construction", "children": [{"id": "2186774b-7d40-4001-ade4-d4aa64e7539b", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit of analysis and temporal boundary"}, {"id": "7103a491-98dd-4ed7-8a73-d53ddb4cdb6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Actors, events, institutions, and outcomes"}, {"id": "5893e7d2-4d25-4517-9b3d-52c7f35f5ed6", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence base and missing voices"}], "description": "Define what the case is a case of and why it matters."}, {"id": "039f85a6-52e4-48e3-b23d-4371c7f90759", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative design", "children": [{"id": "51cda7ff-5611-4701-afbb-01148e22030d", "type": "concept", "title": "Most-similar and most-different comparisons"}, {"id": "cc6d72b9-6dab-40ff-9c82-8d8b7caadb0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive, negative, deviant, and critical cases"}, {"id": "cf6db57c-4acc-4909-8960-57f31dea84f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Within-case process tracing and cross-case matrices"}], "description": "Select cases that illuminate similarities, differences, and mechanisms."}, {"id": "bad98b27-0306-4c22-b31c-550e458f0856", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical context", "children": [{"id": "5b8b59d2-a0af-44e8-b16b-ed58a2e10885", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequence, timing, contingency, and critical junctures"}, {"id": "30f56302-4f7b-4c8d-81e7-133649299431", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional memory and inherited infrastructure"}, {"id": "6edbb7bd-dd7c-4d7a-a134-c2071f333ce2", "type": "concept", "title": "Long-duration processes and presentism"}], "description": "Explain how prior choices shape current possibilities."}, {"id": "88f639cc-5330-4a0b-8ba9-c31c1ef83786", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy and intervention transfer", "children": [{"id": "26af8cde-99a8-4dc9-882d-4e8faf89705f", "type": "concept", "title": "Mechanism versus surface feature"}, {"id": "eda2193a-5ce1-48d2-8ed2-05796440a955", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, culture, politics, resources, and scale"}, {"id": "a4578ba1-37cd-4c96-b887-86f047ab5e7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Adaptation, fidelity, and unintended consequences"}], "description": "Assess whether an apparent success travels across contexts."}, {"id": "ab238921-83cf-4de8-8ef9-c5a22fb76be4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cross-case synthesis", "children": [{"id": "7c6b94dc-2e71-4f2d-a687-3abd295e618d", "type": "concept", "title": "Pattern matching and rival explanations"}, {"id": "de484ad4-6561-4aee-9815-885366d9c1bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope conditions and cautious generalization"}, {"id": "3b39bca3-b1b1-43ad-95c0-df7117313902", "type": "concept", "title": "Lessons, non-lessons, and new questions"}], "description": "Use cases to refine theory and practical judgment."}]}, {"id": "3cb1ea56-831c-4de8-8a4b-d966c74144c2", "type": "topic", "title": "Collaborative Inquiry and Community-Engaged Practice", "description": "Interdisciplinary work depends on collaboration across expertise, status, language, and institutional boundaries. Students learn practical structures for shared inquiry, conflict navigation, and accountable partnership.", "children": [{"id": "dc4ab889-79ff-4028-907b-59fe1b8f067b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Team formation and roles", "children": [{"id": "aa2b2674-ebd7-4f02-b7d1-d96714807ec8", "type": "concept", "title": "Skills and perspective inventory"}, {"id": "70baf5bc-896f-453c-bc8e-ce20dfe0f57e", "type": "concept", "title": "Roles, responsibilities, decision rights, and rotation"}, {"id": "e5c50e3e-08e2-416d-8e1a-b1679416502f", "type": "concept", "title": "Working agreements and psychological safety"}], "description": "Build a team whose diversity is connected to the work."}, {"id": "f2d882ba-36bb-437d-9a9c-00fee0e38a5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Communication across disciplines", "children": [{"id": "e4c46b3c-d497-41a5-83c6-7c68f3cd6368", "type": "concept", "title": "Jargon audits, glossaries, and teach-backs"}, {"id": "4c70713c-f389-4b9e-ac42-7a97c820c54f", "type": "concept", "title": "Questions for clarification versus challenge"}, {"id": "ed338316-4a59-4dce-b3b4-acc473f5b1d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual models and boundary objects"}], "description": "Translate concepts and evidence without oversimplifying."}, {"id": "73e54765-d8e7-464e-b6be-c173469f77e8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collaborative research process", "children": [{"id": "1935dcc6-9a3f-47f7-9dae-4e813bd1bd2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Research questions, task boards, meeting agendas, and decision logs"}, {"id": "b57aaaac-4b10-4cf2-9e9e-85bf46a08822", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared notes, source library, data management, and version control"}, {"id": "7a51bd51-5443-49a3-be3a-aca960e2dcf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Integration checkpoints and peer review"}], "description": "Coordinate interdependent tasks and maintain a shared evidence base."}, {"id": "7d79ee2e-5660-4a61-929b-45a88e9073aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict and disagreement", "children": [{"id": "08e6febf-a5e9-4c3c-a41b-29b59221d167", "type": "concept", "title": "Task, process, relationship, and value conflict"}, {"id": "63ec7a6a-525e-4abc-8ed5-769dd261eb94", "type": "concept", "title": "Active listening, negotiation, and facilitated dialogue"}, {"id": "1de172cd-ff84-4eb7-90c7-9e776070b373", "type": "concept", "title": "Dissent records, escalation, and repair"}], "description": "Use intellectual tension productively while addressing unequal participation."}, {"id": "160246f7-cfaa-4a05-aae8-bdc71caf4c1b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Community partnership", "children": [{"id": "10c88594-099b-4de3-b664-8c249b1c66ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Partner goals, reciprocity, and realistic expectations"}, {"id": "a2a81829-1c8a-4cf9-8be0-bcd099ff81a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible participation and compensation"}, {"id": "3e2e0b48-83f6-4562-80a2-85c61075fa1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback, return of results, sustainability, and exit planning"}], "description": "Co-design the project with people affected by the issue."}]}, {"id": "52a3fa19-ac42-4cc6-900f-a6a34f8429af", "type": "topic", "title": "From Understanding to Action: Design, Foresight, and Evaluation", "description": "Interdisciplinary analysis should inform action without promising a perfect solution. Students learn to develop intervention portfolios, explore alternative futures, evaluate feasibility and consequences, and plan for learning.", "children": [{"id": "5bd747f6-de52-4497-99db-052ac3e91967", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Theory of change", "children": [{"id": "88feb2cf-ec92-4ca5-9c62-13cd63258f74", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem drivers, intervention mechanisms, and assumptions"}, {"id": "19a1de78-74f6-4375-938d-294c1be52bde", "type": "concept", "title": "Causal pathways and enabling conditions"}, {"id": "47ee9af2-ddea-43a3-bbab-4edf5a960a09", "type": "concept", "title": "Indicators, evidence, and rival explanations"}], "description": "Connect activities to outputs, outcomes, and long-term effects."}, {"id": "4e65b9c4-ae0f-4409-a7e9-aa30a412fe5b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Alternative generation", "children": [{"id": "894b8aba-c8c4-47be-90ec-21a7fb7e03c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy, institutional, technological, cultural, and behavioral interventions"}, {"id": "5b2436b2-1273-41aa-b7d0-4ba927fa1823", "type": "concept", "title": "Prevention, mitigation, adaptation, and transformation"}, {"id": "b6d64223-d39f-405c-a4ce-60802d6bbd85", "type": "concept", "title": "Single actions versus coordinated portfolios"}], "description": "Develop multiple strategies at different system levels."}, {"id": "d0373dbf-0164-4f09-a4ae-c7056fa57146", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Futures and scenarios", "children": [{"id": "e0063ec8-66c2-4384-a05d-c37f2484eb82", "type": "concept", "title": "Drivers, critical uncertainties, and scenario logics"}, {"id": "03466286-2ff0-467c-a54b-5f81a4df972b", "type": "concept", "title": "Backcasting and preferred futures"}, {"id": "3e29fe5e-580a-4d1c-9bfa-e4b443f2dfb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Wild cards, signposts, and adaptive pathways"}], "description": "Explore uncertainty rather than extrapolating one expected future."}, {"id": "fee346b1-27f6-4b3c-9a72-972850894ca9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evaluation and tradeoffs", "children": [{"id": "3c2fa96f-2e13-4047-b53e-2cdb21a60028", "type": "concept", "title": "Effectiveness, equity, feasibility, legitimacy, cost, risk, and reversibility"}, {"id": "ac7c72c1-1a6c-4481-8956-96b3cd285a8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Multi-criteria matrices and sensitivity"}, {"id": "fa156a78-a38f-4d1c-8895-15db0bd9ef04", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributional and second-order consequences"}], "description": "Compare options using explicit criteria and multiple stakeholder perspectives."}, {"id": "54523fb3-d7d4-46e4-80c7-8a614c12ddcc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Learning implementation", "children": [{"id": "2231297d-20a1-4100-8e9f-fac34d35a328", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimum viable intervention and staged commitment"}, {"id": "10df10f9-1679-4dcf-b77c-89dbde6d7ac8", "type": "concept", "title": "Monitoring, leading indicators, and stop/pivot/scale rules"}, {"id": "895b4897-fedf-4971-b856-ba87cb8217f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Governance, ownership, resources, and handoff"}], "description": "Design pilots, safeguards, feedback, and revision."}]}, {"id": "20cfd31c-0938-4a90-a262-39ac0866e196", "type": "topic", "title": "Synthesis, Public Communication, and Reflective Integration", "description": "The final module turns interdisciplinary inquiry into a coherent contribution. Students create a public-facing product and an academic synthesis that explain the integrated insight, evidence, uncertainty, ethical commitments, and next steps.", "children": [{"id": "f55138bd-15d0-4192-8934-c34cc43a1369", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interdisciplinary argument", "children": [{"id": "575b91bf-0359-44a6-9a8a-ff78854ab66d", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem statement, disciplinary insights, conflicts, and common ground"}, {"id": "debc8717-d8a9-4ebc-9efa-11d18a33729a", "type": "concept", "title": "Integrated framework and new understanding"}, {"id": "5f6be5fa-7761-41d8-b90c-7a59458d6b54", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence, warrants, counterarguments, and limitations"}], "description": "Build a claim that depends on genuine integration."}, {"id": "7c694ec7-4f21-4da1-87f3-303921ee38da", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genre and audience", "children": [{"id": "07ffe3ec-a333-4106-9177-b1ffaa5b363b", "type": "concept", "title": "Research paper, policy brief, exhibition, documentary, podcast, website, or public forum"}, {"id": "16480167-33ac-4f5b-bb9b-f7b89b99d99b", "type": "concept", "title": "Academic, community, professional, and policy audiences"}, {"id": "94610d9e-d195-4c60-81b6-1474d9059786", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility, language, media, and cultural context"}], "description": "Select forms that fit the people who will use or experience the work."}, {"id": "03226423-5f30-439d-bb3a-70aaffaa0b61", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual and narrative communication", "children": [{"id": "f0f23548-012d-41ab-a4d9-fab5e7c9ad11", "type": "concept", "title": "System maps, timelines, case comparisons, data displays, and scenarios"}, {"id": "e4470d68-b98c-497a-ba88-7519e0e2bc76", "type": "concept", "title": "Story structure, examples, and human experience"}, {"id": "4f1628cf-631d-4df9-b5e4-cda814eb6ef4", "type": "concept", "title": "Source attribution, uncertainty cues, and ethical representation"}], "description": "Make complexity intelligible without flattening uncertainty or disagreement."}, {"id": "8a47fc74-7ae4-4056-a47a-a0baa87c128d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public dialogue and feedback", "children": [{"id": "9a27d0c9-33df-40cf-b06f-02dbd8503594", "type": "concept", "title": "Presentation, facilitation, questions, and listening"}, {"id": "703865ac-ae18-41bf-913f-1daf7b8cb04c", "type": "concept", "title": "Partner review and community response"}, {"id": "e1b4d2b1-1433-4694-8049-7f50fa79886b", "type": "concept", "title": "Revision, accountability, and disagreement"}], "description": "Treat communication as exchange rather than one-way dissemination."}, {"id": "f30482ed-575a-4ff2-9ddb-bb0a0f9a5a40", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reflective integration", "children": [{"id": "17f748c5-d8eb-41a1-b910-2027eab99775", "type": "concept", "title": "Evolution of assumptions and disciplinary identity"}, {"id": "e37565b5-e3fc-4625-8bde-db93a8ee8b49", "type": "concept", "title": "Team process, failures, tensions, and learning"}, {"id": "f00812ef-c571-4055-b25b-cbe95fbdec6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Transfer to future study, citizenship, and work"}], "description": "Articulate how the inquiry changed the student’s thinking and practice."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$intpjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'interdisciplinary-topics-course'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Interdisciplinary Topics Course',
  goal = 'Interdisciplinary Topics Course',
  summary = 'Investigate one consequential “big problem” through multiple disciplinary lenses, integrate diverse evidence into a more comprehensive understanding, and collaborate with relevant publics to create an ethical, useful, and well-communicated contribution.',
  data = $intpjson${"slug": "interdisciplinary-topics-course", "title": "Interdisciplinary Topics Course", "description": "Investigate one consequential “big problem” through multiple disciplinary lenses, integrate diverse evidence into a more comprehensive understanding, and collaborate with relevant publics to create an ethical, useful, and well-communicated contribution.", "topics": [{"id": "3607e0e3-45a4-4d78-a6e9-b50b636f8cc3", "type": "topic", "title": "The Big Question: Defining the Topic and the Problem", "description": "Interdisciplinary inquiry starts with a problem that cannot be understood adequately through one field alone. Students learn to turn a broad theme into a researchable, consequential question with boundaries, stakeholders, and a shared vocabulary.", "children": [{"id": "8a458d9f-9e3a-434e-8b9b-e0faba6362f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Theme and problem space", "children": [{"id": "2297ed0d-0ccf-48bd-9e35-76e6542247dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Possible themes: climate resilience, AI and society, migration, public health, democracy, or urban futures"}, {"id": "ac286a7e-ac70-4414-8c54-a23020ec3aea", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem situations, symptoms, causes, consequences, and contested meanings"}, {"id": "b993113e-2876-46e0-84d8-cf8d8f11b4dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Why the problem exceeds a single discipline"}], "description": "Distinguish a compelling topic from a specific problem that can guide sustained inquiry."}, {"id": "2613ad0b-a52f-4410-bc03-a19fc7625e75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Question formulation", "children": [{"id": "f9bde134-8503-4827-8083-4e527541ac19", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, causal, interpretive, normative, and design questions"}, {"id": "038f0632-85ed-4ff3-afd3-7c252d36f10d", "type": "concept", "title": "Question scope, feasibility, significance, and uncertainty"}, {"id": "16334424-b080-42f2-b7e1-564c8dc92052", "type": "concept", "title": "Nested questions and a shared inquiry agenda"}], "description": "Develop questions that invite explanation, interpretation, evaluation, and action."}, {"id": "0c0f5cc6-aff4-4630-b7d2-b29f431456c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Boundaries and scale", "children": [{"id": "7f4eae34-a740-415c-92ee-af8f431cedad", "type": "concept", "title": "Local, regional, national, planetary, and historical scales"}, {"id": "2b4b7dfa-6d4e-4dea-8608-f952fb4cb20f", "type": "concept", "title": "Population, institution, ecosystem, technology, and time boundaries"}, {"id": "46e44398-4e42-4dfa-9257-f2640cce0379", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundary choices, exclusions, and implications"}], "description": "Decide where the study begins and ends without pretending the problem is isolated."}, {"id": "0c1f41f1-c9b1-4e4d-8e86-27f583bbdeb7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stakeholders and publics", "children": [{"id": "fcf0682f-9439-4f9b-8ea1-c94ff1f083e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Affected communities, decision makers, experts, organizations, and nonhuman interests"}, {"id": "5d02a565-7ea7-45df-b693-a10c81887709", "type": "concept", "title": "Power, voice, incentives, responsibilities, and conflicts"}, {"id": "cace1a00-388b-4389-8e86-2ee6b15f58bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder maps and engagement priorities"}], "description": "Identify who experiences, defines, governs, studies, or can change the problem."}, {"id": "d2b636fc-f110-4c30-8959-df8b1b0a82a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inquiry charter", "children": [{"id": "ed14ca52-621e-4680-b2d3-50a811d875f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Central question, subquestions, outcomes, and audience"}, {"id": "96882ef3-80ac-4418-931b-c46ea1a05bdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Assumptions, terms, unknowns, and success criteria"}, {"id": "5146fca9-1857-44e6-aa5e-5793f1837cd9", "type": "concept", "title": "Research ethics, team norms, milestones, and revision process"}], "description": "Create a living agreement about purpose, evidence, collaboration, and deliverables."}]}, {"id": "03f75b1f-7dc1-4947-9ecb-887d5666c7d4", "type": "topic", "title": "Disciplines, Epistemologies, and Ways of Knowing", "description": "Disciplines are not simply collections of facts; they organize questions, methods, evidence, values, and standards of explanation. Students learn to recognize these architectures so that integration respects real differences rather than flattening them.", "children": [{"id": "def16e24-e29d-4612-b08a-ed5557e64385", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Anatomy of a discipline", "children": [{"id": "05b9639f-baab-4a2c-adac-76ddca905fa4", "type": "concept", "title": "Objects of study and characteristic questions"}, {"id": "2aa4df97-9674-44a6-bf9f-d8c043481dae", "type": "concept", "title": "Core concepts, theories, methods, genres, and institutions"}, {"id": "66c6e693-8cad-497d-adfd-9e30f78d0a0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards of evidence, explanation, and expertise"}], "description": "Examine how fields define legitimate problems and knowledge."}, {"id": "50260d02-cba2-4ef3-ba95-f7758c44ae46", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Epistemologies", "children": [{"id": "be2c24e6-3e13-49bc-be25-6b16fe67a2a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Empiricism, interpretation, rationalism, pragmatism, and critical approaches"}, {"id": "367ac869-8e58-4abe-861f-31fd282154a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Objectivity, situated knowledge, standpoint, and reflexivity"}, {"id": "7b0dc2c1-5421-4bd7-8bc3-87d89e50b18b", "type": "concept", "title": "Certainty, probability, ambiguity, and pluralism"}], "description": "Compare accounts of what can be known and how claims become warranted."}, {"id": "eb7883dc-b9a5-46df-a930-6133c478fc8e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Paradigms and assumptions", "children": [{"id": "f13d6b61-5d9d-4781-a9f1-800ca5a5b722", "type": "concept", "title": "Ontology, causality, agency, structure, and scale"}, {"id": "b7ade903-6e6e-48c3-b23b-6d209d3a7082", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual, institutional, cultural, ecological, and technological explanations"}, {"id": "0ea036f1-7c72-45e4-b605-1ccde04a522f", "type": "concept", "title": "Normal science, anomalies, and paradigm change"}], "description": "Surface commitments that are often invisible within a field."}, {"id": "7698a4e7-58f8-427e-972e-ac4af02b9fdc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multi-, inter-, and transdisciplinarity", "children": [{"id": "e5f7bbc9-9aea-4dc6-b478-e891be75c3a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Multidisciplinary juxtaposition"}, {"id": "f7b27ece-4585-4e37-ab86-5216f2217917", "type": "concept", "title": "Interdisciplinary synthesis"}, {"id": "7841489c-8ca7-4494-86a6-c0b5861ff1ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Transdisciplinary collaboration with practitioners and communities"}], "description": "Differentiate parallel contributions from genuine integration and co-production."}, {"id": "660913ec-4f0b-4af2-bd8c-7df52ffce4a9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intellectual humility", "children": [{"id": "4aa2b85f-fec7-4177-8d30-de47e8d8889b", "type": "concept", "title": "Competence boundaries and responsible borrowing"}, {"id": "88b5d870-5ab2-4477-b470-7945bc55bd69", "type": "concept", "title": "Translation without caricature"}, {"id": "377047a1-1e20-4386-b11a-a821d2f62c59", "type": "concept", "title": "Productive disagreement and revisable conclusions"}], "description": "Treat expertise as necessary but partial."}]}, {"id": "88a60149-f800-4d19-813f-bc87a696fec3", "type": "topic", "title": "Humanities Lenses: Meaning, History, Culture, and Interpretation", "description": "Humanities methods reveal how language, memory, values, narratives, and cultural forms shape complex problems. Students learn to analyze meaning and historical possibility rather than treating present conditions as natural or inevitable.", "children": [{"id": "bd1cb5f9-5d1c-4e7d-ac95-8c8273d91f62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical inquiry", "children": [{"id": "0085c64c-e340-49f7-b698-bf3bcd1bec20", "type": "concept", "title": "Periodization, chronology, and turning points"}, {"id": "f9dfb0d5-1f16-4ac4-b9d0-6e956b40f53a", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and secondary sources"}, {"id": "663784e1-73ec-4177-a7de-f72cd35b4926", "type": "concept", "title": "Archives, silences, and historiography"}], "description": "Trace change, continuity, contingency, and path dependence."}, {"id": "7e433cf9-e22b-44ba-8d1d-72873e13bc6c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Textual and rhetorical analysis", "children": [{"id": "3e00ff98-d33f-48a9-9704-172bfcd881a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Close reading and contextual interpretation"}, {"id": "29f5b998-3a65-4408-8a63-37e18443da4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Metaphor, framing, genre, argument, and audience"}, {"id": "fe546bee-871c-4b4c-8fd2-955ecb08a334", "type": "concept", "title": "Public discourse, policy language, and media narratives"}], "description": "Study how language constructs problems, identities, and possible actions."}, {"id": "1e145080-2960-45c1-b73a-2526b437e71b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cultural analysis", "children": [{"id": "84f71dfa-39c6-45e2-a315-c70379f24293", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation, identity, ritual, memory, and ideology"}, {"id": "4c620dc1-9fa5-4f8a-aa4d-816afde42d53", "type": "concept", "title": "Popular culture, material culture, and digital culture"}, {"id": "8453b4e0-7bc7-4f8e-9f43-ab5dfd4e1a1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Dominant, residual, emergent, and countercultural forms"}], "description": "Interpret symbols, practices, institutions, and everyday life."}, {"id": "14548717-472c-4d0e-a75a-fc58bcfb05db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Philosophical analysis", "children": [{"id": "882acf20-34d0-4222-83a1-82a52b5f7283", "type": "concept", "title": "Conceptual distinctions and thought experiments"}, {"id": "d6879176-c17f-4fa2-becf-4fb03a8f7a96", "type": "concept", "title": "Normative theories and practical ethics"}, {"id": "dd4c395c-bb1f-4e59-b25d-aea1b3c7de62", "type": "concept", "title": "Logic, counterargument, and reflective equilibrium"}], "description": "Clarify concepts and evaluate reasons, values, and obligations."}, {"id": "0d76129d-d050-4006-b55e-28c497661618", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Creative and imaginative knowledge", "children": [{"id": "23648f30-feff-4a1e-8e68-0f4713f9034b", "type": "concept", "title": "Literature, visual art, performance, and film as evidence or inquiry"}, {"id": "1b796ecd-c18c-478f-b113-ac4d7b552c9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Speculative fiction and alternative futures"}, {"id": "36562d23-e9d2-4c7f-819a-d6a69097821d", "type": "concept", "title": "Aesthetic form, empathy, estrangement, and interpretation"}], "description": "Use art and narrative to explore experience, possibility, and moral attention."}]}, {"id": "60875113-f172-4f0c-9961-6304a53034fc", "type": "topic", "title": "Social Science Lenses: Institutions, Behavior, Power, and Society", "description": "Social sciences connect individual action to groups, institutions, markets, policies, and cultures. Students compare explanatory models and learn to combine qualitative and quantitative evidence without confusing association with cause.", "children": [{"id": "22579864-2e96-4647-82f2-133df96c8b39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Levels of social explanation", "children": [{"id": "ac986965-c208-4d6c-b957-062913538412", "type": "concept", "title": "Micro, meso, and macro levels"}, {"id": "f88743fd-37fb-4d60-91ea-124e20e0f4fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency, structure, norms, incentives, and identity"}, {"id": "265c7370-5be5-4804-8dca-283d43f0e912", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback between individual and collective outcomes"}], "description": "Locate mechanisms across persons, networks, organizations, and institutions."}, {"id": "eb371b0d-9a17-4c30-ab60-91bc3cb4f094", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutions and governance", "children": [{"id": "de32633c-7109-4615-80e4-a985a90138b3", "type": "concept", "title": "States, markets, firms, schools, families, and civil society"}, {"id": "f1ec7860-9590-4d81-a201-72b976aa5618", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy design, implementation, and administrative capacity"}, {"id": "cfd608b4-51b9-4610-9a1a-71026ce75855", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional change, lock-in, and legitimacy"}], "description": "Analyze how formal and informal rules distribute authority and resources."}, {"id": "5398a17f-8e60-44cc-a419-19c2696d551f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Power and inequality", "children": [{"id": "74afdd13-cb86-4492-92e9-f58578c127e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Class, race, gender, disability, citizenship, and intersectionality"}, {"id": "dc588487-b683-465c-866c-4a4bf986379f", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural, relational, discursive, and coercive power"}, {"id": "6e7ffee5-4afb-4d91-bf37-d56249844ef8", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement, lived experience, and cumulative disadvantage"}], "description": "Examine how benefits, burdens, recognition, and voice are distributed."}, {"id": "38042057-f16a-481c-8146-ac8d5c27d42b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Behavior and decision making", "children": [{"id": "31b53e74-dc8a-4320-8724-48e0c3efdc2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Preferences, incentives, heuristics, and biases"}, {"id": "6a044e4e-5e67-4c10-ab40-15134d21c8db", "type": "concept", "title": "Social norms, networks, identity, and collective action"}, {"id": "c87a88a0-5430-4530-a6d1-db0010c738a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Experiments, surveys, observational studies, and limitations"}], "description": "Study choice in social context rather than assuming fully rational actors."}, {"id": "e02e022d-f602-43d7-8a2f-df0e90a095d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Causal and comparative reasoning", "children": [{"id": "55353d05-1259-44d5-99da-9904b63172dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Correlation, mechanism, confounding, and counterfactuals"}, {"id": "a2152e0d-52d8-470e-943e-cf033b3ad865", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative case selection"}, {"id": "ada7b3ce-1ee5-4311-881f-8c8abd457170", "type": "concept", "title": "Generalization, context, and external validity"}], "description": "Evaluate why outcomes differ across groups, places, institutions, or time."}]}, {"id": "34fca065-59f4-4b10-bc95-8036ef882572", "type": "topic", "title": "Natural and Quantitative Lenses: Systems, Measurement, and Evidence", "description": "Scientific and quantitative approaches help characterize mechanisms, patterns, constraints, and uncertainty. Students learn to use numbers critically—checking definitions, models, uncertainty, and values embedded in measurement.", "children": [{"id": "4f19591c-7602-4b1d-bae8-6ce1becfaacb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scientific modeling", "children": [{"id": "a20ac08a-1d5d-4134-8b1f-6045c9676181", "type": "concept", "title": "Variables, mechanisms, assumptions, boundaries, and scales"}, {"id": "06a2e984-31c7-4871-bcdc-fb51622fd816", "type": "concept", "title": "Conceptual, mathematical, computational, and physical models"}, {"id": "bccadfbd-b2e6-427e-b44c-67caefec275b", "type": "concept", "title": "Model validation, limitations, and domain of applicability"}], "description": "Represent selected features of reality to explain or predict."}, {"id": "7312ff2a-f6dd-44a4-8f1b-754ddf26e24d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Measurement and indicators", "children": [{"id": "f2e8915a-670d-438a-a71d-9895a579904b", "type": "concept", "title": "Operational definitions, units, validity, and reliability"}, {"id": "02f19da2-bff1-4253-ae11-dfc264b5060a", "type": "concept", "title": "Proxies, composite indicators, baselines, and denominators"}, {"id": "d7341517-eb93-45ae-b5ca-952d39e81958", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement error and missing data"}], "description": "Ask what a number represents, how it was produced, and what it excludes."}, {"id": "aee53cb9-b85b-4872-bc02-209a578774a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data interpretation", "children": [{"id": "da644f46-73b6-4f52-ae93-6acd8dda3b60", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributions, rates, uncertainty intervals, and effect sizes"}, {"id": "5173db02-84fb-4ecb-b535-9ed4eeb39563", "type": "concept", "title": "Correlation, causation, selection, and survivorship"}, {"id": "a865edc9-1f0f-4aad-8828-2de0b020541f", "type": "concept", "title": "Visualization choices and misleading comparisons"}], "description": "Read patterns while resisting overclaiming."}, {"id": "044b68c7-b628-4866-b7f5-17598a495344", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ecological and planetary constraints", "children": [{"id": "8fd4cfa4-3741-40fd-8ffb-70e4ccea7977", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy and material flows"}, {"id": "c4a1320a-5d0a-49a8-9974-b953f3b0f0b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecosystems, resilience, thresholds, and feedback"}, {"id": "be0cb7fc-606d-4519-a11f-53d26f2b5c96", "type": "concept", "title": "Climate, biodiversity, pollution, and resource use"}], "description": "Connect human systems to biophysical processes and limits."}, {"id": "66475f0c-9f90-4a99-ab8a-0476cf48d01c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quantification and values", "children": [{"id": "646a7781-0652-4892-af8f-0de2ddbc40b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefit, harm, risk, and quality-of-life metrics"}, {"id": "76882da4-3921-4b6a-9b72-745378b8a111", "type": "concept", "title": "Monetization and nonmonetary values"}, {"id": "471c3268-095f-460d-bfb9-c4a1d24bd029", "type": "concept", "title": "Distribution, uncertainty, and ethical limits of aggregation"}], "description": "Recognize that deciding what to count is partly normative."}]}, {"id": "12d69e6c-462d-4bad-bcae-c9507e2a41a0", "type": "topic", "title": "Arts, Design, and Creative Practice as Inquiry", "description": "Creative practice can generate knowledge, reveal experience, and prototype alternatives. Students learn to use design and artistic methods alongside—not merely after—analysis.", "children": [{"id": "0465a89d-76a9-4477-9045-05ce6a2c4fb0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Practice-based inquiry", "children": [{"id": "a69e05d0-7c3d-45dc-9981-ab029f3d9cca", "type": "concept", "title": "Sketching, composing, performance, fabrication, and iteration"}, {"id": "a4f55be8-202f-42fb-a10a-ae00309bb3e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Process documentation and reflective commentary"}, {"id": "15e7af25-9327-4f73-9d9b-4846e3b9c5b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Tacit, embodied, sensory, and experiential knowledge"}], "description": "Treat making as a disciplined process of questioning and discovery."}, {"id": "826e3304-d034-4d22-925d-8bd00d37026d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Human-centered research", "children": [{"id": "d815e015-84b4-497f-98a3-1662147f4310", "type": "concept", "title": "Observation, interviews, journey maps, and cultural probes"}, {"id": "91cbf49e-3a96-4043-bdf5-e7ebc49bf246", "type": "concept", "title": "Extreme users, accessibility, and inclusive participation"}, {"id": "d80d2264-f9bc-4ff2-bf0a-e73bc15bb117", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, reciprocity, and avoiding extractive research"}], "description": "Understand needs and contexts through direct engagement."}, {"id": "facc9f3a-ad41-4bb9-8834-3ed0793426c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Problem reframing", "children": [{"id": "bd7e95b7-23ea-4bb8-b6d3-c1383659b24f", "type": "concept", "title": "How-might-we questions and assumption reversal"}, {"id": "0cfda1c4-20f6-4c45-82b9-669be036e6cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Needs, values, functions, and systemic causes"}, {"id": "bb735a72-cfbd-493b-abbd-145215fbcfaa", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternative framings and their consequences"}], "description": "Challenge inherited definitions and expand the space of possibilities."}, {"id": "a77dbe9e-71d8-4522-82c6-a1bcd125c478", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ideation and prototyping", "children": [{"id": "85647dc9-41b1-4938-ab42-eb3f5b044893", "type": "concept", "title": "Divergence, analogy, combination, and co-creation"}, {"id": "5f657ba2-9e83-4858-b5d4-362c87906feb", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-fidelity prototypes, storyboards, scenarios, and role-play"}, {"id": "0a81fcd6-a9a5-49a1-adf2-52f932f2d8fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback, iteration, and learning goals"}], "description": "Make ideas tangible enough to test and discuss."}, {"id": "8d4d91e3-8e09-498d-8acd-ea81cc94f807", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation and public imagination", "children": [{"id": "56bee263-ed02-4d28-af5e-35f26b78f574", "type": "concept", "title": "Exhibitions, maps, installations, documentary, and interactive media"}, {"id": "5e73781f-ffbc-4b8e-94e7-df7ad7c6b386", "type": "concept", "title": "Counter-narratives and speculative design"}, {"id": "79faf836-7fd0-4216-bdf7-a5aa082420e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience experience, accessibility, and interpretation"}], "description": "Use form and media to shape attention and collective possibility."}]}, {"id": "1e0a05f0-801b-42c5-84b4-03738fb6a803", "type": "topic", "title": "Evidence Literacy and Mixed-Methods Research", "description": "World-class interdisciplinary work is methodologically plural but not methodologically vague. Students learn to locate, assess, combine, and document qualitative, quantitative, historical, and creative evidence.", "children": [{"id": "7b3b9a28-6984-4d89-9c20-4a7ce8c99c45", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research strategy", "children": [{"id": "5d0965e3-10f2-41ce-b2f2-23894532105d", "type": "concept", "title": "Exploratory, descriptive, explanatory, evaluative, and design research"}, {"id": "9911055a-4c20-4bb6-a43a-fa235e20379e", "type": "concept", "title": "Case study, comparative, experimental, ethnographic, archival, and mixed-methods designs"}, {"id": "336b7a78-a879-4953-a0a7-ba31ae3bd13c", "type": "concept", "title": "Feasibility, access, ethics, and triangulation"}], "description": "Match questions to evidence and methods."}, {"id": "d94b5ea9-127c-42aa-9d43-742dac3b7cae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Source discovery and provenance", "children": [{"id": "e4a9a6e3-0cf6-4c04-bdcd-dd2c8b69782d", "type": "concept", "title": "Scholarly databases, archives, datasets, policy documents, and community knowledge"}, {"id": "5936f298-3140-49b2-a8f8-1683da61d676", "type": "concept", "title": "Citation chaining, controlled vocabulary, and grey literature"}, {"id": "994fc4f0-44be-4b42-9cea-2c091784a947", "type": "concept", "title": "Authorship, funding, version, date, and data lineage"}], "description": "Build a transparent evidence base across disciplines."}, {"id": "1c2081fb-0cf6-4753-8c9f-8d9feea8763b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical appraisal", "children": [{"id": "22e39e53-16bf-4ce1-8805-5a50551b3745", "type": "concept", "title": "Credibility, relevance, validity, reliability, and bias"}, {"id": "fcf3eb2c-efcb-40b9-a124-c15deebc417d", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer review, replication, saturation, and corroboration"}, {"id": "0844955c-4523-4c7c-a73e-b15cb18c3f35", "type": "concept", "title": "Expert consensus, disagreement, and uncertainty"}], "description": "Evaluate evidence using standards appropriate to its source and claim."}, {"id": "bca65af8-f40b-4654-8dd8-fe109a8581aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mixed-methods integration", "children": [{"id": "d3c52a52-9cde-4b5c-a9f8-dd93cee3b422", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequential, concurrent, and embedded designs"}, {"id": "0835883b-a6fc-4940-99c1-691db2d0ec75", "type": "concept", "title": "Convergence, complementarity, expansion, and contradiction"}, {"id": "e60d7cf0-a31a-43e7-8dd0-a985d0cc518b", "type": "concept", "title": "Joint displays and integrated interpretation"}], "description": "Use methods to answer complementary parts of the problem."}, {"id": "85ce0ba8-a758-4a2d-bb8b-d2282fef1c39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research transparency", "children": [{"id": "3807bf38-8b55-4d77-8ccd-d3d09bd00883", "type": "concept", "title": "Search logs, coding decisions, analytic memos, and data dictionaries"}, {"id": "64b803a2-00ac-4efd-9cba-e3bb5bbd5c69", "type": "concept", "title": "Citation management and reproducible workflows"}, {"id": "49c7f9ad-9601-46be-a3b3-b169662e315f", "type": "concept", "title": "Open materials, privacy, intellectual property, and limitations"}], "description": "Make the path from source to conclusion inspectable."}]}, {"id": "63e801ba-d5e9-445f-8a0e-001849eb5e5f", "type": "topic", "title": "Systems Thinking, Complexity, and Mapping", "description": "Complex problems emerge from interactions, feedback, delays, adaptation, and multiple scales. Students learn to map systems without mistaking the map for the world and to identify leverage, tradeoffs, and unintended consequences.", "children": [{"id": "069264af-7930-4fca-bd35-fd060b56c150", "type": "subtopic", "title": "System structure", "children": [{"id": "6cbc8523-c282-4ebc-a5f8-e57328e159cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Stocks, flows, actors, institutions, technologies, and environments"}, {"id": "e7a709c0-c5eb-4589-a371-3900971e305c", "type": "concept", "title": "Material, information, financial, and influence connections"}, {"id": "c62d9434-96df-472c-8463-2835b77ca093", "type": "concept", "title": "Nested systems and boundary critique"}], "description": "Define elements, relationships, purpose, and boundary."}, {"id": "afb654df-bfb0-408a-a9bd-f4b6a8159525", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Feedback and dynamics", "children": [{"id": "46846b6c-ccd0-4555-9ece-a3fc65d259dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Reinforcing and balancing loops"}, {"id": "94d49948-3687-4097-b303-e1a9c1ec6eda", "type": "concept", "title": "Delays, accumulation, nonlinearity, and oscillation"}, {"id": "dd36dbfd-b859-4614-b191-78fe54c18fcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Path dependence, lock-in, and tipping behavior"}], "description": "Explain how circular causality creates persistence or change."}, {"id": "17290319-fe3f-4071-a092-e06c4f279050", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Networks and emergence", "children": [{"id": "ad1cce04-4567-4061-802b-416914634d3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Nodes, ties, centrality, clustering, and diffusion concepts"}, {"id": "bceb699e-68b6-4146-848c-113724cd2d4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Local rules and emergent outcomes"}, {"id": "79a9af60-69af-4d05-af63-b886fc76ffb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Contagion, coordination, polarization, and resilience"}], "description": "Study patterns that arise from distributed interaction."}, {"id": "3587ddf7-cdd1-4ed0-9034-8b53b97505ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Complex adaptive systems", "children": [{"id": "4b9437fc-df62-4b2b-9993-28cbfe89429e", "type": "concept", "title": "Agents, variation, selection, and adaptation"}, {"id": "fcf941df-7b36-4083-8e16-8932de69bd77", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-organization and regime shifts"}, {"id": "52398aeb-568b-46f7-b2ad-646e6d893486", "type": "concept", "title": "Prediction limits and scenario thinking"}], "description": "Recognize learning, adaptation, heterogeneity, and coevolution."}, {"id": "febec7f9-88e5-4a21-9f4e-f1b80d3f2e23", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Leverage and unintended effects", "children": [{"id": "8fa2026d-8a74-4ae2-aafc-73f889fd74ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Parameters, information, rules, goals, and paradigms"}, {"id": "2434f5ab-b52f-46e0-8962-e4eb075091d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Second-order effects and policy resistance"}, {"id": "e7b30a37-8047-4020-8cf1-cc1ac3d2efc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Robust portfolios and monitoring signals"}], "description": "Identify interventions while examining who gains, who loses, and what might rebound."}]}, {"id": "91eca66b-4276-447a-9f9f-8ffc568c8139", "type": "topic", "title": "Integration: Creating Common Ground and New Understanding", "description": "Integration is the defining intellectual work of interdisciplinarity. Students learn to connect insights by clarifying concepts, reconciling assumptions, relating mechanisms, and constructing a synthesis that changes how the problem is understood.", "children": [{"id": "a6460ff0-8908-4ba3-a706-1d47320a246e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict mapping", "children": [{"id": "662c39a8-e496-47ba-ba86-441c37eb31c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Different terms for similar ideas"}, {"id": "3ae8b5ab-b253-4bff-a385-670c7c6e74ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Same terms with different meanings"}, {"id": "31d5e5e1-92c0-4756-b821-575369bb24eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Differences in scale, unit of analysis, method, or value"}], "description": "Locate where disciplinary findings agree, complement, or contradict."}, {"id": "5263db01-99c1-49fd-9e2a-098d2d720b7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Concept clarification", "children": [{"id": "0bd71003-f5e8-44e9-bb1a-ff1abdc19eb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Definitions, dimensions, typologies, and boundary concepts"}, {"id": "e70424dd-88d6-4fa2-a64b-a8ebe5422f34", "type": "concept", "title": "Common ground and conceptual translation"}, {"id": "3920c550-3e77-4172-a99c-f0139cb51690", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundary objects and trading zones"}], "description": "Create enough shared language for collaboration without erasing productive difference."}, {"id": "28484c2c-d801-4f81-875f-1c51bd9aca6c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integration techniques", "children": [{"id": "326cf6ec-8168-4272-bfbf-26f788209a54", "type": "concept", "title": "Extension, redefinition, organization, transformation, and causal linkage"}, {"id": "657198b9-0e9f-4604-ba7d-3ba91ff0944b", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept maps, matrices, timelines, and multi-level models"}, {"id": "f9cbdbe6-60c4-43e0-8018-d1b88893bee3", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative, systems, and design synthesis"}], "description": "Combine disciplinary insights through explicit reasoning."}, {"id": "a2ee4bb9-2903-466d-891f-52e0f1231e03", "type": "subtopic", "title": "More-comprehensive understanding", "children": [{"id": "586ce664-1a20-483a-bdc3-7032dc8d5ae7", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-level mechanisms and interactions"}, {"id": "820dae38-b834-4c16-8e5b-1fff14a25217", "type": "concept", "title": "Tradeoffs, tensions, paradoxes, and conditional conclusions"}, {"id": "e20a1ad2-dc29-4952-956f-00fed1dca145", "type": "concept", "title": "Novel hypotheses, questions, and intervention points"}], "description": "Show what the integration explains that separate accounts do not."}, {"id": "eeb6954d-728b-4d6a-b3e5-a375064d8f4f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integration quality", "children": [{"id": "e7c8ed78-dead-4f9e-b280-78693b52fa69", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsiveness to each discipline’s strongest evidence"}, {"id": "b56a3f12-1a8e-45ea-9def-99e35bf53761", "type": "concept", "title": "Coherence, explanatory power, usefulness, and transparency"}, {"id": "ebdeb130-84f7-4504-abdc-dafa015997fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Residual disagreement and limits"}], "description": "Evaluate synthesis rather than rewarding mere breadth."}]}, {"id": "a6c0ea30-a345-42ec-b926-785264a9316c", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Power, Positionality, and Responsible Inquiry", "description": "Interdisciplinary projects make choices about whose knowledge counts, who bears risk, and what futures are desirable. Students learn to examine their own position, engage ethically, and make normative commitments visible.", "children": [{"id": "75d1865b-eace-43b5-87bf-e5b827b01578", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Positionality and reflexivity", "children": [{"id": "9482d64c-1847-48d0-b1e5-b726216ec197", "type": "concept", "title": "Researcher standpoint and access"}, {"id": "94aa4952-2f8e-4ac9-a678-84cc5d293184", "type": "concept", "title": "Insider/outsider roles"}, {"id": "225c799f-1efd-4387-b287-8a1ea7b0985b", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflexive journals and team discussion"}], "description": "Understand how identity, training, interests, and institutional location shape inquiry."}, {"id": "59566e67-6a94-418e-9684-1ee2f586e35e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research and engagement ethics", "children": [{"id": "a740a11b-7ed0-4d5f-857d-4998aedfa3de", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, confidentiality, privacy, and data stewardship"}, {"id": "ac5f461c-782e-4fb0-8951-16119bab556a", "type": "concept", "title": "Community knowledge, ownership, compensation, and attribution"}, {"id": "d7d8447b-2d79-4218-bfe1-3d540c23c131", "type": "concept", "title": "Human-subjects review and harm assessment"}], "description": "Protect people and communities while building reciprocal relationships."}, {"id": "abd60437-7739-404c-89a9-24ecc97f2563", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Justice frameworks", "children": [{"id": "2a097a15-27a1-49b3-b957-f5d58ce526b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Procedural, distributive, restorative, and intergenerational justice"}, {"id": "9ae8451b-89a5-47f1-b6c5-851239d5387f", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental, disability, racial, gender, and data justice"}, {"id": "3bceb33a-6c05-40aa-9823-8364cf19405e", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectionality and cumulative impacts"}], "description": "Evaluate distribution, recognition, participation, and capability."}, {"id": "98936213-b9aa-40cd-8cf1-4fda9cadc963", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Knowledge and power", "children": [{"id": "ce0bc7b0-25b5-4db0-b0c3-63acf2a96f8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Epistemic injustice and testimonial credibility"}, {"id": "819857d6-cb70-44bf-8fc5-d6bdffe3574d", "type": "concept", "title": "Coloniality, extraction, and Indigenous knowledge sovereignty"}, {"id": "a13559a8-3bd5-490c-940b-9f0ffcd5d8ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional expertise and democratic participation"}], "description": "Examine how expertise becomes authoritative and how alternatives are marginalized."}, {"id": "9dccd136-a4e6-45fd-9d55-425197900cd1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible recommendations", "children": [{"id": "10ca5742-0d58-4eea-a0fb-b8a0c75d3a8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefits, burdens, reversibility, and precaution"}, {"id": "c2be98fe-c6e8-493e-aef1-34dba3e463f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflicts of interest and accountability"}, {"id": "331054b8-60cf-481d-a131-5437c59bccc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Conditions, safeguards, monitoring, and avenues for redress"}], "description": "State values, uncertainties, and tradeoffs rather than hiding them behind technical language."}]}, {"id": "acb7a97f-2355-4da3-b623-e4f342911e5e", "type": "topic", "title": "Comparative Case Studies and Historical Context", "description": "Cases let students test concepts against real complexity. Comparison reveals patterns, causal mechanisms, contextual differences, and the danger of copying solutions without understanding where they came from.", "children": [{"id": "2cc844f3-69ab-4b53-bed6-c37eb140ac31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case construction", "children": [{"id": "2186774b-7d40-4001-ade4-d4aa64e7539b", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit of analysis and temporal boundary"}, {"id": "7103a491-98dd-4ed7-8a73-d53ddb4cdb6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Actors, events, institutions, and outcomes"}, {"id": "5893e7d2-4d25-4517-9b3d-52c7f35f5ed6", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence base and missing voices"}], "description": "Define what the case is a case of and why it matters."}, {"id": "039f85a6-52e4-48e3-b23d-4371c7f90759", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative design", "children": [{"id": "51cda7ff-5611-4701-afbb-01148e22030d", "type": "concept", "title": "Most-similar and most-different comparisons"}, {"id": "cc6d72b9-6dab-40ff-9c82-8d8b7caadb0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive, negative, deviant, and critical cases"}, {"id": "cf6db57c-4acc-4909-8960-57f31dea84f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Within-case process tracing and cross-case matrices"}], "description": "Select cases that illuminate similarities, differences, and mechanisms."}, {"id": "bad98b27-0306-4c22-b31c-550e458f0856", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical context", "children": [{"id": "5b8b59d2-a0af-44e8-b16b-ed58a2e10885", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequence, timing, contingency, and critical junctures"}, {"id": "30f56302-4f7b-4c8d-81e7-133649299431", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional memory and inherited infrastructure"}, {"id": "6edbb7bd-dd7c-4d7a-a134-c2071f333ce2", "type": "concept", "title": "Long-duration processes and presentism"}], "description": "Explain how prior choices shape current possibilities."}, {"id": "88f639cc-5330-4a0b-8ba9-c31c1ef83786", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy and intervention transfer", "children": [{"id": "26af8cde-99a8-4dc9-882d-4e8faf89705f", "type": "concept", "title": "Mechanism versus surface feature"}, {"id": "eda2193a-5ce1-48d2-8ed2-05796440a955", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, culture, politics, resources, and scale"}, {"id": "a4578ba1-37cd-4c96-b887-86f047ab5e7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Adaptation, fidelity, and unintended consequences"}], "description": "Assess whether an apparent success travels across contexts."}, {"id": "ab238921-83cf-4de8-8ef9-c5a22fb76be4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cross-case synthesis", "children": [{"id": "7c6b94dc-2e71-4f2d-a687-3abd295e618d", "type": "concept", "title": "Pattern matching and rival explanations"}, {"id": "de484ad4-6561-4aee-9815-885366d9c1bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope conditions and cautious generalization"}, {"id": "3b39bca3-b1b1-43ad-95c0-df7117313902", "type": "concept", "title": "Lessons, non-lessons, and new questions"}], "description": "Use cases to refine theory and practical judgment."}]}, {"id": "3cb1ea56-831c-4de8-8a4b-d966c74144c2", "type": "topic", "title": "Collaborative Inquiry and Community-Engaged Practice", "description": "Interdisciplinary work depends on collaboration across expertise, status, language, and institutional boundaries. Students learn practical structures for shared inquiry, conflict navigation, and accountable partnership.", "children": [{"id": "dc4ab889-79ff-4028-907b-59fe1b8f067b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Team formation and roles", "children": [{"id": "aa2b2674-ebd7-4f02-b7d1-d96714807ec8", "type": "concept", "title": "Skills and perspective inventory"}, {"id": "70baf5bc-896f-453c-bc8e-ce20dfe0f57e", "type": "concept", "title": "Roles, responsibilities, decision rights, and rotation"}, {"id": "e5c50e3e-08e2-416d-8e1a-b1679416502f", "type": "concept", "title": "Working agreements and psychological safety"}], "description": "Build a team whose diversity is connected to the work."}, {"id": "f2d882ba-36bb-437d-9a9c-00fee0e38a5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Communication across disciplines", "children": [{"id": "e4c46b3c-d497-41a5-83c6-7c68f3cd6368", "type": "concept", "title": "Jargon audits, glossaries, and teach-backs"}, {"id": "4c70713c-f389-4b9e-ac42-7a97c820c54f", "type": "concept", "title": "Questions for clarification versus challenge"}, {"id": "ed338316-4a59-4dce-b3b4-acc473f5b1d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual models and boundary objects"}], "description": "Translate concepts and evidence without oversimplifying."}, {"id": "73e54765-d8e7-464e-b6be-c173469f77e8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collaborative research process", "children": [{"id": "1935dcc6-9a3f-47f7-9dae-4e813bd1bd2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Research questions, task boards, meeting agendas, and decision logs"}, {"id": "b57aaaac-4b10-4cf2-9e9e-85bf46a08822", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared notes, source library, data management, and version control"}, {"id": "7a51bd51-5443-49a3-be3a-aca960e2dcf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Integration checkpoints and peer review"}], "description": "Coordinate interdependent tasks and maintain a shared evidence base."}, {"id": "7d79ee2e-5660-4a61-929b-45a88e9073aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict and disagreement", "children": [{"id": "08e6febf-a5e9-4c3c-a41b-29b59221d167", "type": "concept", "title": "Task, process, relationship, and value conflict"}, {"id": "63ec7a6a-525e-4abc-8ed5-769dd261eb94", "type": "concept", "title": "Active listening, negotiation, and facilitated dialogue"}, {"id": "1de172cd-ff84-4eb7-90c7-9e776070b373", "type": "concept", "title": "Dissent records, escalation, and repair"}], "description": "Use intellectual tension productively while addressing unequal participation."}, {"id": "160246f7-cfaa-4a05-aae8-bdc71caf4c1b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Community partnership", "children": [{"id": "10c88594-099b-4de3-b664-8c249b1c66ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Partner goals, reciprocity, and realistic expectations"}, {"id": "a2a81829-1c8a-4cf9-8be0-bcd099ff81a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible participation and compensation"}, {"id": "3e2e0b48-83f6-4562-80a2-85c61075fa1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback, return of results, sustainability, and exit planning"}], "description": "Co-design the project with people affected by the issue."}]}, {"id": "52a3fa19-ac42-4cc6-900f-a6a34f8429af", "type": "topic", "title": "From Understanding to Action: Design, Foresight, and Evaluation", "description": "Interdisciplinary analysis should inform action without promising a perfect solution. Students learn to develop intervention portfolios, explore alternative futures, evaluate feasibility and consequences, and plan for learning.", "children": [{"id": "5bd747f6-de52-4497-99db-052ac3e91967", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Theory of change", "children": [{"id": "88feb2cf-ec92-4ca5-9c62-13cd63258f74", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem drivers, intervention mechanisms, and assumptions"}, {"id": "19a1de78-74f6-4375-938d-294c1be52bde", "type": "concept", "title": "Causal pathways and enabling conditions"}, {"id": "47ee9af2-ddea-43a3-bbab-4edf5a960a09", "type": "concept", "title": "Indicators, evidence, and rival explanations"}], "description": "Connect activities to outputs, outcomes, and long-term effects."}, {"id": "4e65b9c4-ae0f-4409-a7e9-aa30a412fe5b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Alternative generation", "children": [{"id": "894b8aba-c8c4-47be-90ec-21a7fb7e03c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy, institutional, technological, cultural, and behavioral interventions"}, {"id": "5b2436b2-1273-41aa-b7d0-4ba927fa1823", "type": "concept", "title": "Prevention, mitigation, adaptation, and transformation"}, {"id": "b6d64223-d39f-405c-a4ce-60802d6bbd85", "type": "concept", "title": "Single actions versus coordinated portfolios"}], "description": "Develop multiple strategies at different system levels."}, {"id": "d0373dbf-0164-4f09-a4ae-c7056fa57146", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Futures and scenarios", "children": [{"id": "e0063ec8-66c2-4384-a05d-c37f2484eb82", "type": "concept", "title": "Drivers, critical uncertainties, and scenario logics"}, {"id": "03466286-2ff0-467c-a54b-5f81a4df972b", "type": "concept", "title": "Backcasting and preferred futures"}, {"id": "3e29fe5e-580a-4d1c-9bfa-e4b443f2dfb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Wild cards, signposts, and adaptive pathways"}], "description": "Explore uncertainty rather than extrapolating one expected future."}, {"id": "fee346b1-27f6-4b3c-9a72-972850894ca9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evaluation and tradeoffs", "children": [{"id": "3c2fa96f-2e13-4047-b53e-2cdb21a60028", "type": "concept", "title": "Effectiveness, equity, feasibility, legitimacy, cost, risk, and reversibility"}, {"id": "ac7c72c1-1a6c-4481-8956-96b3cd285a8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Multi-criteria matrices and sensitivity"}, {"id": "fa156a78-a38f-4d1c-8895-15db0bd9ef04", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributional and second-order consequences"}], "description": "Compare options using explicit criteria and multiple stakeholder perspectives."}, {"id": "54523fb3-d7d4-46e4-80c7-8a614c12ddcc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Learning implementation", "children": [{"id": "2231297d-20a1-4100-8e9f-fac34d35a328", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimum viable intervention and staged commitment"}, {"id": "10df10f9-1679-4dcf-b77c-89dbde6d7ac8", "type": "concept", "title": "Monitoring, leading indicators, and stop/pivot/scale rules"}, {"id": "895b4897-fedf-4971-b856-ba87cb8217f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Governance, ownership, resources, and handoff"}], "description": "Design pilots, safeguards, feedback, and revision."}]}, {"id": "20cfd31c-0938-4a90-a262-39ac0866e196", "type": "topic", "title": "Synthesis, Public Communication, and Reflective Integration", "description": "The final module turns interdisciplinary inquiry into a coherent contribution. Students create a public-facing product and an academic synthesis that explain the integrated insight, evidence, uncertainty, ethical commitments, and next steps.", "children": [{"id": "f55138bd-15d0-4192-8934-c34cc43a1369", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interdisciplinary argument", "children": [{"id": "575b91bf-0359-44a6-9a8a-ff78854ab66d", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem statement, disciplinary insights, conflicts, and common ground"}, {"id": "debc8717-d8a9-4ebc-9efa-11d18a33729a", "type": "concept", "title": "Integrated framework and new understanding"}, {"id": "5f6be5fa-7761-41d8-b90c-7a59458d6b54", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence, warrants, counterarguments, and limitations"}], "description": "Build a claim that depends on genuine integration."}, {"id": "7c694ec7-4f21-4da1-87f3-303921ee38da", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genre and audience", "children": [{"id": "07ffe3ec-a333-4106-9177-b1ffaa5b363b", "type": "concept", "title": "Research paper, policy brief, exhibition, documentary, podcast, website, or public forum"}, {"id": "16480167-33ac-4f5b-bb9b-f7b89b99d99b", "type": "concept", "title": "Academic, community, professional, and policy audiences"}, {"id": "94610d9e-d195-4c60-81b6-1474d9059786", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility, language, media, and cultural context"}], "description": "Select forms that fit the people who will use or experience the work."}, {"id": "03226423-5f30-439d-bb3a-70aaffaa0b61", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual and narrative communication", "children": [{"id": "f0f23548-012d-41ab-a4d9-fab5e7c9ad11", "type": "concept", "title": "System maps, timelines, case comparisons, data displays, and scenarios"}, {"id": "e4470d68-b98c-497a-ba88-7519e0e2bc76", "type": "concept", "title": "Story structure, examples, and human experience"}, {"id": "4f1628cf-631d-4df9-b5e4-cda814eb6ef4", "type": "concept", "title": "Source attribution, uncertainty cues, and ethical representation"}], "description": "Make complexity intelligible without flattening uncertainty or disagreement."}, {"id": "8a47fc74-7ae4-4056-a47a-a0baa87c128d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public dialogue and feedback", "children": [{"id": "9a27d0c9-33df-40cf-b06f-02dbd8503594", "type": "concept", "title": "Presentation, facilitation, questions, and listening"}, {"id": "703865ac-ae18-41bf-913f-1daf7b8cb04c", "type": "concept", "title": "Partner review and community response"}, {"id": "e1b4d2b1-1433-4694-8049-7f50fa79886b", "type": "concept", "title": "Revision, accountability, and disagreement"}], "description": "Treat communication as exchange rather than one-way dissemination."}, {"id": "f30482ed-575a-4ff2-9ddb-bb0a0f9a5a40", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reflective integration", "children": [{"id": "17f748c5-d8eb-41a1-b910-2027eab99775", "type": "concept", "title": "Evolution of assumptions and disciplinary identity"}, {"id": "e37565b5-e3fc-4625-8bde-db93a8ee8b49", "type": "concept", "title": "Team process, failures, tensions, and learning"}, {"id": "f00812ef-c571-4055-b25b-cbe95fbdec6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Transfer to future study, citizenship, and work"}], "description": "Articulate how the inquiry changed the student’s thinking and practice."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$intpjson$::jsonb,
